Relevant paths are `Assets/Scripts/Save/CheckpointRestore.cs`, `Assets/Scripts/Session/GameSession.cs`, `Assets/Scripts/Inventory/InventoryModel.cs`, and `Assets/Scripts/Scenes/SceneBootstrapper.cs`. The restore service and scene bootstrapper both survive scene changes. Here is the reduced code from the current branch:

```csharp
private async void OnSceneLoaded(Scene scene, LoadSceneMode mode)
{
    if (!scene.name.StartsWith("Level_")) return;
    await _save.RestoreAsync(_session.CurrentSlot, destroyCancellationToken);
    _inventory.Apply(_save.CurrentSnapshot.Items);
}

public async Task RestoreAsync(string slot, CancellationToken token)
{
    var json = await File.ReadAllTextAsync(PathFor(slot), token);
    var snapshot = JsonUtility.FromJson<SaveSnapshot>(json);
    CurrentSnapshot = snapshot;
    SnapshotRestored?.Invoke(snapshot);
}
```

